statement:
Fix a subset $S\subseteq[n]$ of coordinates. For every point $x$ of the Boolean hypercube $\{0,1\}^n$ and every coordinate $i\in[n]$, the value of the Walsh--Fourier character $\chi_S$ at the point $x^i$ obtained by flipping the $i$-th coordinate of $x$ is
\[
  \chi_S(x^i) \;=\;
  \begin{cases} -\chi_S(x) & i\in S,\\[2pt] \chi_S(x) & i\notin S. \end{cases}
\]

replaced:
Flipping coordinate $i$ negates $\chi_S$ when $i\in S$ and leaves it unchanged
otherwise:
\[
  \chi_S(x^i) \;=\;
  \begin{cases} -\chi_S(x) & i\in S,\\ \chi_S(x) & i\notin S. \end{cases}
\]
